  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Implement Prefix Cache Matching and Reuse** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\ndef inference_prefix_cache_reuse(prompt_tokens: list, cached_block_tokens: list, block_size: int = 4) -> dict:\n    p, bs = list(prompt_tokens), int(block_size)\n    m_blocks = 0\n    for i in range(len(p) // bs):\n        blk = p[i*bs:(i+1)*bs]\n        if i < len(cached_block_tokens) and cached_block_tokens[i] == blk: m_blocks += 1\n        else: break\n    reused = m_blocks * bs\n    return {'matched_blocks': m_blocks, 'reused_tokens': reused, 'new_tokens_to_compute': len(p) - reused}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
